This directory contains files necessary to generate bootable images (PXE and USB) for FBOSS using the kiwi ng tool.

KIWI NG Documentation:
    https://osinside.github.io/kiwi/overview.html

KIWI NG XML Schema:
    https://github.com/OSInside/kiwi.git

    Steps to validate schema changes:
        1) Clone the above repository
        2) xmllint --relaxng  kiwi/kiwi/schema/kiwi.rng <templates/centos-09.0/config.xml>

The directories here are:

    bin         - executable scripts that do the real work
    lib         - helper code that is common across scripts
    logs        - all logs go here
    templates   - kiwi-ng image templates
    output      - all build output go here (USB ISO and PXE Boot tarball)

image_builder/bin:
    build_image_in_container.sh     - Script that builds the image inside docker container

image_builder/templates:
    Contains the template(s) that contain the information needed by kiwi-ng-3
    to generate
        centos-09.0     - CentOS-9.0 based FBOSS image template files

image_builder/output:
    All generated output goes into this directory

To build a PXE bootable image the steps are as follows:

    1) Use the distro_cli tool to build the image:
        git clone git@github.com:nexthop-ai/private-fboss.git <wsdir>
        cd <wsdir>/fboss-image
        ./distro_cli/fboss-image build <manifest.json>

    This will generate the distribution files specified in the manifest, typically:
        FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.install.tar       - PXE bootable tarball
        FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.install.iso       - Bootable USB ISO image

    Extract contents of the above tarball in tftp directory: /vol/shared/images/tftp/FBOSS-Distro-Image, it should appear as follows:

        ctikku@ds102:/vol/shared/images/tftp/FBOSS-Distro-Image$ ls -la
        total 1028520
        drwxr-xr-x  2 ctikku ctikku      4096 Oct 22 17:41 .
        drwxrwxrwx 11 root   root        4096 Oct 22 01:36 ..
        -rw-r--r--  1 ctikku ctikku       102 Oct 22 17:33 FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.append
        -rw-r--r--  1 ctikku ctikku        79 Oct 22 17:34 FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.config.bootoptions
        -rw-r--r--  1 ctikku ctikku  77611554 Oct 22 17:33 FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.initrd
        -rw-r--r--  1 ctikku ctikku 526592000 Oct 22 17:40 FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.install.tar
        lrwxrwxrwx  1 ctikku ctikku        44 Oct 22 17:33 FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.kernel -> pxeboot.FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.kernel
        -rw-r--r--  1 ctikku ctikku        78 Oct 22 17:33 FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.sha256
        -rw-r--r--  1 ctikku ctikku 354188456 Oct 22 17:30 FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.xz
        -rw-r--r--  1 ctikku ctikku  79692563 Oct 22 17:34 pxeboot.FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.initrd
        -rwxr-xr-x  1 ctikku ctikku  15075368 Oct 22 17:33 pxeboot.FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.kernel
        ctikku@ds102:/vol/shared/images/tftp/FBOSS-Distro-Image$

    The three files we care about are are properly named and are:
        pxeboot.FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.kernel
        pxeboot.FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.initrd
        FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.xz

The Grub entry for FBOSS needs to be as follows:

    set wwwserverip="10.11.12.13"
    consoleargs="console=ttyS4,57600n8 nomodeset"

    menuentry "FBOSS Distro Image (version x.y.z)" {

        echo "Installing FBOSS Distro Image (version x.y.z)"

        # Directory where the image files are located, relative to wwwserverip html root
            set imagedir="images/tftp/FBOSS-Distro-Image-x.y.z"

        # The three files that we need that are generated by kiwi-ng
            set kernel="pxeboot.FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.kernel"
            set initrd="pxeboot.FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.initrd"
            set xzImage="FBOSS-Distro-Image.x86_64-1.0.xz"

        set xzFile="http://${wwwserverip}/${imagedir}/${xzImage}"

        echo -n '   Loading kernel ... '
        linux   (http)/${imagedir}/${kernel} ${consoleargs} \
                rd.neednet=1 \
                rd.kiwi.install.pxe \
                ip=eno1:dhcp \
                ipv6.disable=1 \
                rd.kiwi.install.image=${xzFile} \
                rd.kiwi.install.target=/dev/nvme0n1

        echo "done"
        echo -n '   Loading initrd ... '
        initrd  (http)/${imagedir}/${initrd}
        echo "done"
    }
